  "text_md": "0.1 0.1\n0.05 0.05 0 0 -0.05-0.05 -0.1-0.1 -0.1-0.05 0 0.05 0.1-0.1-0.05 0 0.05 0.1\n(a) Interpolation nodes (b) Center evaluation nodes\nFigure 1: Distribution of interpolation and evaluation nodes within a circle of radius 0.1.\n\n(a) Error in *f* vs. shape parameter (b) Error in *fx* vs. shape parameter\n\n||(c) Error in f||vs. shape parameter|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Figure 2:|Comparison of Accuracy and Numerical Stability for HRBF and MHRBF: The errors (function,|||\n|derivatives, f with polynomial degree of 6 and n = 4 for MHRBF.|and f|) and condition number computed in double precision for GA kernel, as functions of shape parameter ε,||\n\n*y* (d) Condition number vs. shape parameter *f*, and its first *x y*\n\nThe results inFigure 2reveal significant accuracy improvements with MHRBF compared to HRBF. Since the error trends for *∇f* closely follow that of *f*, the subsequent analysis focuses primarily on the function interpolation.Figure 2ademonstrates that the MHRBF achieves low error over a large range of *ε* values, *−*14 with the error *∼* 10 for all *ε* ≳ 0*.*5, despite the fact that the condition number of the MHRBF being\n",
